# Theory notes

**Reference:** `notes/numerical/theory/fraction-division.md`

## Where files live

- Path: `notes/{area}/theory/{topic}.md`
- `{area}`: `numerical`, `verbal`, or `spatial` (CCAT areas)
- `{topic}`: kebab-case English slug (e.g. `fraction-division`, `percent-change`)

Create the `theory/` folder only when adding real content.

## File template

Follow this section order. Rename headings to fit the topic, but keep the same flow and tone.

```markdown
# {Topic Title}

**Area:** {area} — theory
**Added:** YYYY-MM-DD

## What it means
(one-sentence intuition — what question this concept answers)

---

## {Core method or main trick}
(procedure, numbered steps, worked example)

**One-line rule:** *short memorable sentence*

---

## Why it works (intuition)
(concrete analogy — pizza slices, chocolate bar, etc.)

---

## Step-by-step examples
### Example 1: `{expression}`
(numbered steps)
### Example 2: `{expression}`
(numbered steps)

---

## Extra tricks
(optional subsections — shortcuts, mental math, edge cases)

---

## Common mistakes
| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| ... | ... |

---

## Pocket summary
```
{compact formula or rule}
```
1. ...
```

## Format rules

- **English only** in persisted content (chat may be Portuguese)
- **No LaTeX** — use plain math in backticks: `3/4`, `1 1/2`, `a/b × c/d` (standard markdown preview)
- Separate major sections with `---`
- Keep notes **short, scannable, actionable** — no fluff
- Use **bold** for key terms; *italics* for one-line rules and guiding questions
- Worked math and expressions: inline code (backticks), not `$...$` or `\(...\)`
- Pocket summary: fenced code block for the compact rule, then a short numbered checklist
- Common mistakes: table with concrete wrong vs right examples when applicable

## Do not

- Duplicate course/session notes — theory files teach the concept; link out instead of copying drill logs
- Skip metadata (`Area`, `Added`) or the pocket summary
- Invent empty `theory/` folders under every area
